    "module": {
      "purpose": "Defines the bitmask flag constants and composite masks used by React's fiber reconciler to track side effects, fiber states, and commit-phase work. Provides a typed Flags number and exports individual bits, reused aliases, and phase masks conditioned on feature flags.",
      "summary": "This module is a central constants file for the React reconciler. It declares a Flow type alias for flag bits and then exports dozens of numeric bitmask constants representing fiber effects (Placement, Update, ChildDeletion), static tags (LayoutStatic, PassiveStatic), and dev-only markers. Several constants alias existing bits because they are mutually exclusive per fiber type. Composite masks (MutationMask, LayoutMask, PassiveMask, StaticMask, BeforeMutationMask) union relevant bits to let the commit phase skip subtrees without effects. Two masks are composed conditionally using imported feature flags, enabling event-handle and effect-event APIs. The values of the first bits are frozen for React DevTools compatibility.",
      "businessContext": "Core internal rendering engine definitions for React. Incorrect flag bits would break commit-phase effect application and DevTools inspection, causing silent UI divergence or crashes.",
